    "snippet": "---\ntitle: The shocking real-life age differences between 35 fictional parents and their children\nauthor: Gabbi Shaw\ndate: 2023-06-24\n---\n- Meryl Streep, who just turned 74, is only three years younger than Cher, her mother in \"Mamma Mia.\"\n\n- This isn't the only example of onscreen kids and parents being comically close in age.\n\n- Amy Poehler is only seven years older than her \"Mean Girls\" daughter Rachel McAdams.\n\nHollywood is notorious for casting 25-year-old high-schoolers who have 37-year-old parents. We've compiled 35 of the most egregious parent-child age gaps in Hollywood history, including an on-screen mom who is years younger than her on-screen sons and an on-screen mother and son who were so close in age they began dating in real life.\n\nKeep scrolling to see more of the shocking age gaps.\n\nSean Connery played Harrison Ford's dad in \"Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade,\" but they were only 12 years apart.\n\nAt the time of release, Ford was 47 and and Connery was 59 \u2014 though, somehow, it's never unbelievable when Connery calls Ford \"Junior.\"\n\nIn \"Outer Banks,\" Big John is actually only 13 years older than John B., as played by 43-year-old Charles Halford and 30-year-old Chase Stokes.\n\nYes, Stokes is 30 years old playing a 17-year-old \u2014 and he's not the only one on \"Outer Banks\" playing older.\n\nMandy Moore is younger than all three of the adult versions of her kids \u2014 Chrissy Metz, Sterling K. Brown, and Justin Hartley \u2014 on \"This Is Us.\"\n\nOn \"This Is Us,\" a show which jumps around multiple different time periods, Moore played Rebecca Pearson, the matriarch of the Pearson clan and mother to Randall (Brown), Kate (Metz), and Kevin (Hartley).\n\nAnd though Moore rocked impeccable old age makeup when she was seen in the current time, it's still funny to realize that she, at 39, is younger than 47-year-old Brown, 46-year-old Hartley, and 42-year-old Metz.\n\nHer on-screen husband, Milo Ventimiglia, falls in the middle of his kids at 45.\n\nBonus: She's also younger than on-screen daughter-in-law Beth, played by a 41-year-old Susan Kelechi Watson and her son-in-law Toby, played by 42-year"
