    "snippet": "---\ntitle: MovieWeb\nauthor: Meaghan Argueta\ndate: 2024-10-13\n---\nWhen you read a book, or watch a drama, can you picture the characters in your head? Do you think about certain actors that could play the roles in a potential book-to-film adaptation? Screenwriters and casting directors may do this on their own time, but they also have to do it professionally. When it comes to casting a film, some actors have to line up and go through the audition process, and some desperately wait by the phone to hear back from their agency. Then there are those big name A-listers who don't have to audition because either a part was written specifically for them, or the director wants their particular acting skills and name attached to the movie.\n\nThese big names are people like Adam Sandler, Emma Stone, Will Smith, Meryl Streep, and dozens of others. They are people everyone immediately recognizes, so there is no IMDb search happening while the movie is rolling. When a film is made with all of these great actors, more people are likely to watch it due to their love for certain individuals. Plus, knowing that some of the biggest names in Hollywood banded together for a film is pretty amazing. With that said, check out these 20 movies with the most star-studded casts.\n\nUpdated October 12, 2024: This collection of star-studded films has been updated with additional information, including where to stream each movie featured.\n\n20 Valentine's Day (2010)\n\nValentine's Day shows this day can be hectic for many different reasons, and this star-studded cast makes the romantic holiday feel like a roller coaster of emotions. An ensemble cast stitches a series of interconnected stories together in just a little over two hours, featuring everything between dramatic connections and sappy romantic gestures. With so many incredible people on set, it's unfortunate that the reviews for this film were significantly lower than expected, even though it was certainly a smash hit at the box office.\n\nWho's In Valentine's Day?\n\nAshton Kutcher plays a florist that proposes and gets rejected by Jessica Alba's character. Jennifer Garner plays a woman who falls in love with a dreamy doctor played by Patrick Dempsey. Taylor Swift and Taylor Lautner portray high school sweeties who are just figuring out their relationship. Other notable actors include Julia Roberts, Bradley Cooper, Jessica Biel, George Lopez, and Anne Hathaway. Stream Valentine's Day on Hoopla.\n\n19 The Rid"
