    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Movie Genres & Subgenres | Definition, Types & Examples\ndate: 2023-11-21\n---\nMovie Genres & Subgenres | Definition, Types & Examples\n\nHow many types of movie genres are there?\n\nIt is impossible to say exactly how many movie genres there are. There is a huge amount of overlap between genres and not all critics and audiences agree on how to categorize film genres and subgenres.\n\nWhat are the main movie genres?\n\nSome of the most common film genres include drama, comedy, science fiction, fantasy, horror, thriller, western, and musical. Each of these genres has its own subgenres.\n\nHow many movie genres are there?\n\nThere are dozens of movie genres that have different characteristics. There is no definitive list or ranking that determines exactly how many genres there are.\n\nWhat are the different types of film?\n\nIn the broadest terms, most films are either comedies or dramas. However, in many cases, it is helpful to further categorize films into genres like horror or fantasy to more clearly differentiate them.\n\nFilm Genres: Deeper Dives\n\nThis lesson introduced you to the concept of film genres and subgenres as a way of categorizing and understanding what different films are going for. Use the following prompts to think more deeply about these concepts.\n\nA Matter of Opinion\n\nThis lesson already gave you a few questions to consider, like why some people love horror movies while others hate them, and why romantic comedies remain popular. Consider the genres listed here as well as other genres like science fiction, drama, thriller, mystery, and historical fiction, and even nonfiction genres like documentaries and biopics. Which ones do you enjoy the most, and why? Create a list ranking each genre and include your comments on each one: what typifies this genre? What do you like or dislike about it? This will help you in the next prompt.\n\nUnderstanding Subgenres\n\nNow that you have your list, take the top three film genres that you enjoy the most. For instance, think about what kinds of subgenres make up each type. Write a detailed list of as many subgenres as you think are relevant and list the characteristics of each one. For a really detailed look at subgenres, choose just one or two and do more detailed research. When did that genre or subgenre originate? Which films are considered part of the genre? How does it interact with other kinds of film? Does this genre or subgenre extend to other kinds of media, like novels or music? Answer"
